  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HelpAge 2015-2019 - HelpAge (New strategy 2018-2022)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">HelpAge 2015-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core funding support to HelpAge International for the implementation of their 2015-2020 strategy. HelpAge operates in 62 low- and middle income countries in order to   improve the living condition for people over 60 years old. The support is based on the rights-, health - as well as the poverty perspective. The global development of older peoples rights and       safety net is the main focus.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till HelpAge International f&#xf6;r implementering av deras strategi 2015-2020. HelpAge International &#xe4;r ett sekretariat (inkl. HK-London, sju regionala kontor och 14 landkontor) f&#xf6;r ett hundratal medlemsorganisationer (Affiliates) runt om i v&#xe4;rlden. HelpAge International &#xe4;r den enda globala organisationen som arbetar specifikt med &#xe4;ldre m&#xe4;nniskors r&#xe4;ttigheter som r&#xe4;tten till  h&#xe4;lsov&#xe5;rd, sociala trygghetssystem samt r&#xe4;tten att leva ett v&#xe4;rdigt liv utan v&#xe5;ld. Sidas st&#xf6;d kommer bidra till genomf&#xf6;randet av HelpAges strategi f&#xf6;r perioden 2015-2018. HelpAges strategiska m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r en v&#xe4;rld d&#xe4;r &#xe4;ldre kvinnor och m&#xe4;n kan s&#xe4;ga: 1) jag har den inkomst jag beh&#xf6;ver; 2) jag f&#xe5;r den b&#xe4;sta m&#xf6;jliga v&#xe5;rd jag beh&#xf6;ver; 3) jag &#xe4;r trygg, fri fr&#xe5;n all diskriminering och v&#xe5;ld; samt 4) min r&#xf6;st &#xe4;r h&#xf6;rd.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2015-2020&#xa0;strategy contains a series of outcomes under the four areas below. In 2018, gender and disability under inclusion have been added to the results framework as areas of particular focus.1. I have the income I need
i. More older people will have access to adequate, sustainable minimum pensions as part of a social protection floorii. More households containing older people will be able to maintain, adapt or increase their income and food security2. I enjoy the best possible health and care, well being and dignity
i. More older people will report better health, and well-being and more older people living in isolation, or with chronic conditions and frailty, will be supported to live well in a place of their choice.ii. More older people will be supported to prepare for and withstand the impact of shocks in their lives, livelihoods and health3. I am safe and secure, free from all forms of discrimination, violence and abuse
i. Older people will have significantly better access to legal and other support services relating to violence and abuseii. More older people will be supported to prepare for and withstand the impact of shocks in their lives, livelihoods and health4. My voice is heard
i. More older people will be able to participate in decision-making processes that will improve life in old age now and in the futureii. Significant progress will be made towards a convention on the rights of older peopleiii. The UN, governments, donors and other bodies will adopt age-inclusive policies and programmes, responding to the commitments of the post-2015 Sustainable Development Goals and of international humanitarian law
5. Inclusion: Gender and Disability
i. Influencing on gender and ageingii. Collecting data that includes everyoneiii. Influencing on ageing and disabilityiv. Strengthening gender and disability inclusion</narrative>
  </description>
